From 2a5def4efcccc8a17f0878f92a22f2815154a8e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:36:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 101/274] TileLang V4.1 MoE: the combine adds the shared
 expert's output when it runs first

With the FP32 combine (one rounding of each rank's partial) the combine wrote an
FP32 partial that the runner read back to add the shared expert's BF16 output and
round: twice the combine's output bytes, then an add kernel over them. When the
shared expert runs before the routed experts (no stream overlap: steps past the
shared-stream threshold, the sequence-parallel prefill), the runner now hands its
output to the TileLang experts, whose combine adds it to the slot-order FP32 sum
and rounds once to BF16. The runner then skips its add.

The bits are the runner's: the same FP32 add and one round-to-nearest-even, so a
row's result does not depend on which path its step takes. Decode steps keep the
shared expert on its stream and the runner's add.

